  "status_text": "Twelve readings can recover more than a thousand hidden weights from one board. Eleven readings cannot always do it. Draw ten separate two-by-two blocks. Each block has two ways to match its rows to its columns, giving 1,024 whole-board matchings. The weight of each is the product of the entries it picks. A reading changes the entries by chosen complex multipliers and takes a determinant. At 22:14 UTC Lean checked that eleven fixed readings and one chosen after seeing them recover every weight, and that eleven fail even with feedback (L-lib-1093).",
